          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            is
            %strong compact
            if its underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+group"} compact topological group
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#maximal_tori Maximal tori
          %p
            All
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal tori
            of a compact Lie group are conjugate by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+automorphisms"} inner automorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            of a maximal torus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            of a compact Lie group is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+Lie+group"} rank
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalizer"} normalizer
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(T)
            of a maximal torus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            determines
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+group"} Weyl group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(G)=W(G,T)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with respect to a choice of a maximal torus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+automorphisms"} group of automorphisms
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            which are restrictions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+automorphisms"} inner automorphisms
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            The maximal torus is of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+of+a+subgroup"} index
            in its normalizer; the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(T)/T
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(G)
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(G)
            for a compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homogeneous+space"} homogeneous space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/T
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+variety"}> flag variety
            ”).
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+compact+Lie+groups+and+reductive+algebraic+groups"} relation between compact Lie groups and reductive algebraic groups
          %h3#AbelianCompactLieGroups Abelian compact Lie groups
          %p
          #MaximalToriOfConnectedCompactLieGroupsAreMaximalAbelianSubgroups.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal torus
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
              is also the maximal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
          (e.g.
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Salamon21"} Salamon 2021, Lem. 6.5
          %p
            In particular:
          #ConnectedCompactLieGroupsAreTori.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              All connected compact abelian Lie groups are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tori"} tori
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          (
          %a{:href => "#Adams82"}> Adams 1982, Thm. 2.19, Cor. 2.20
          )
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Classification of compact abelian Lie groups)
              %br/
              Assuming the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product+group"} direct product group
              of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-torus"} n-torus
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G_{\mathrm{e}}
                    \\xhookrightarrow{\;\;}
                    G
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
              in the given compact abelian Lie group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConnectedCompactLieGroupsAreTori"}
              this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G_{\mathrm{e}}
                    \\,\simeq\,
                    T^n
            %p
              hence its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/divisible+group"} divisible group
              and therefore, by
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "injective+object#InjectiveAbelianGroupIsDivisibleGroup"} this Prop.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} injective object
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extension
